            "review_title": "Review at Kimchi Restaurant",
            "review_text": "GlobalKuidaore\nAsia380 contributions\n0\nGreat Seafood Pancakes(Pajeon)!\nFeb 2018 • Couples\nYes, the prices are high, compared to local Vietnamese food, but Kimchi’s seafood pancake is worth 240k dong! It’s one of the best Korean seafood pancakes we’ve ever had. It’s big enough to feed two people. Of course, it comes with banchan, which is pretty good, too. We didn’t think their bulgogi was very good. Cold noodles(naengmyon) were pretty average, but will satisfy your craving. \n\nThe Korean owner (lady) is friendly. They also take credit cards. This is a great place to visit if you want to take a break from Vietnamese food. We’ll definitely be back for Pajeon next year (we spend two months out of the year in Nha Trang.)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 12, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
